  "post": {
    "caption": "The ring that switches hands. In Germany, the wedding ring goes on the right ring finger, while the engagement ring starts on the left, and many couples move it over to the right after the wedding. The Orthodox Church traditionally has wedding rings on the right hand, and in the ceremony the rings are exchanged three times. Austria and Poland also wear wedding rings on the right, but in the US and UK it goes on the left, and Dutch Catholics wear it on the left while Protestants wear it on the right. Nobody can say for sure why Germany switched. France and Italy wear wedding rings on the left hand.",
